 LLM powered systems. Both are written here. And that is why we can say that there are two types of LLM evals. One is called model evals and the second is application evals. Model evals work is very simple. Given, evaluating LLM and application evals is to evaluate LLM based applications. And if this distinction is clear in your mind in the beginning, then it is very good.\", \"evals are different for Latency and all types of metrics. In the last video, we discussed what are the different eval methods through which we perform evaluations. We discussed three things in this video. Programmatic methods, LLMEvalse-based as a judge, and how to perform eval with humans. In nutshell, this is the summary of whatever we have covered in this course till now. In today's video, we are going to discuss a very important topic. The topic is Offline Eval vs Online Eval. First, I will tell you what is offline eval, then I will tell you what is online eval, and then what are the differences between them. We will see that and you will learn a lot in this process. This is our agenda for today. This is the topic that we are going to cover today. Is it clear till now? What have we\", \"is worth deploying or not, then we call the evals that you run there as offline eval. As simple as that. So, everything that you have read till now, everything comes under offline eval. So, we didn't learn anything new. We gave a new name to what we had learned in the past. So, quickly tell me in the chat that if someone asks you tomorrow what offline evals are, would you be able to answer? Can you explain offline eval? Okay. Easy, right? Now, let's discuss an important aspect of offline eval. I want to hear from you. You tell me what is the main purpose of offline eval? If there is more than one purpose, then what is it? Type it once and tell me. What are the main purposes of an offline eval? Why do we need an offline eval? Why don't we make an LLM based software and deploy it directly?\", \"running or no