e the generator code generator is basically an LLM in which you give a question and relevant context and that generator gives you an answer in return so we\"]}": {"cached_metrics_data": [{"metric_data": {"name": "Contextual Recall", "threshold": 0.7, "success": true, "score": 1.0, "reason": "The score is 1.00 because the sentence discusses the evaluation process of a retriever, including metrics such as recall and precision, which aligns well with the provided supportive reasons.", "strictMode": false, "flaky": false, "evaluationModel": "Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "evaluationCost": 0, "verboseLogs": "Verdicts:\n[\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": \"The sentence discusses the evaluation process of a retriever, including metrics such as recall and precision.\",\n        \"expected_output\": \"The retriever is evaluated using recall and precision. Recall measures how many of the relevant documents the retriever managed to fetch, and precision measures how many of the fetched documents were actually relevant.\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": \"The sentence mentions the importance of relevance in retrieving documents.\",\n        \"expected_output\": \"The retriever is evaluated using recall and precision. Recall measures how many of the relevant documents the retriever managed to fetch, and precision measures how many of the fetched documents were actually relevant.\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": \"The sentence talks about setting up a testing environment for LLM evaluations.\",\n        \"expected_output\": \"The retriever is evaluated using recall and precision. Recall measures how many of the relevant documents the retriever managed to fetch, and precision measures how many of the fetched documents were actually relevant.\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": \"The sentence describes the role of a retriever in a larger application.\",\n 