 his training process basically how much world knowledge is hidden in his weights and biases his parametric knowledge is a way to test knowledge capability and this is the most important capability think about it when the LLMs were trained for the first time on this massive internet scale data then the expectation would be that if we ask about anything on the internet then it will tell us so knowledge capability is like the most fundamental capability that an LLM can have\", \"write yes we will start ok so yeah, first of all we will discuss MMLU because this is the mother of all benchmarks at least in knowledge capability this is the mother of all benchmarks this is where things originated, so as I said the specialty of this benchmark is breadth of knowledge this simply tests one thing of LLM that how much breadth of knowledge it has not depth of knowledge, but breadth of knowledge and to do this in this benchmark over 57 subjects, 14000 multiple choice questions data set was made and from where this data set was taken where these questions have come from, real exams USMLE, USGRE, AP and other people have also sourced from their side now obviously it must have been taken from the internet from the text book, but yeah the main idea is that 57 subjects, 14000 questions MCQs ok, it was launched in September 2020 and it had only one job to tell how smart is a given LLM, smart in terms of how much knowledge it has, ok from 2021 to 2024 all the LLMs that have\"]}": {"cached_metrics_data": [{"metric_data": {"name": "Faithfulness", "threshold": 0.7, "success": false, "score": 0.5, "reason": "The score is 0.50 because the actual output partially contradicts the retrieval context due to minor discrepancies that do not significantly impact overall alignment.", "strictMode": false, "flaky": false, "evaluationModel": "Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "evaluationCost": 0, "verboseLogs": "Truths (limit=None):\n[\n    \"MMLU is the mother of all benchmarks in knowledge capability.\",\n