": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": \"This statement provides context about the limitations of relying solely on more data for knowledge retention.\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"no\",\n        \"reason\": \"This statement discusses the uniqueness of each LLM and does not directly relate to the question asked.\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": \"This statement touches upon the variability in model performance due to different factors, which indirectly relates to the question.\"\n    }\n]"}, "metric_configuration": {"threshold": 0.7, "evaluation_model": "Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "strict_mode": false, "include_reason": true}}]}, "{\"actual_output\": \"When logging production conversations, you should store the following information:\\n\\n1. **Conversation ID**: Each conversation is assigned a unique identifier.\\n2. **Timestamp**: The time at which the conversation occurred.\\n3. **User Name**: The name of the user who initiated the conversation.\\n4. **Message Content**: The text of the message.\\n5. **User Actions**: Actions taken by the user (e.g., typing, clicking buttons).\\n6. **User Input**: User input received from the chatbot.\\n7. **Chatbot Response**: Chatbot's response to the user.\\n8. **User Feedback**: User's feedback or responses to\", \"context\": null, \"expected_output\": null, \"hyperparameters\": null, \"input\": \"what information should i store when logging production conversations?\", \"retrieval_context\": [\"store the question that the user asked. What context was generated in the rag chat bot in the process of answering that question? I will store that context in the chat bot. I will store the output that the chat bot gave on the basis of that context and question. Apart from that, I will store a lot of operational things such as latency in milliseconds, how many tokens were spent in the prompt, how many completion tokens are there, how much total cost was spent, did any error come? If an error came, what is its status code? I will store all this. Apart from this, if the user is giving me some other signals, I will store those signals too. Like if there is a behavioral metric such as he is pressing thumbs up or thumbs down during the conversation, then I will store that too. Is he mailing? He is saying that I don't want to talk to you, I want to talk to a human or give my email ID, I want to mail. So if the matter is escalating, I will store that. The user is asking the same questions\", \"want to talk to a human or give my email ID, I want to mail. So if the matter is escalating, I will store that. The user is asking the same questions again and again because he feels that the chat bot is not helping him, he is rephrasing the question. So I will store all these things. Everything will be stored. Can someone tell me a tool to store all this? Have you seen a tool in the past where you use that tool to store such things? Perfect. Amin was right. I had also taught on YouTube, we had covered in detail that we had made a chat bot and we were storing every conversation of that chat bot. Where? On Langsmith. I can show you right now. So see this. This is Langsmith. Langsmith has different projects. What can you do in those projects? All your conversations are there. These are all conversations. You can store those conversations. You store everything in it. What the user sent, what was your output, there is a lot of metadata. Everything is stored. So this is kept with you. Now\"]}": {"cached_metrics_data": [{"metric_data": {"name": "Faithfulness", "threshold": 0.7, "success": false, "score": 0.1, "reason": "The score is 0.10 because the actual output does not match any of the provided contradictions.", "strictMode": false, "flaky": false, "evaluationModel": "Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "evaluationCost": 0, "verboseLogs": "Truths (limit=None):\n[] \n \nClaims:\n[\n    \"Logging production conversations involves storing various pieces of information such as Conversa