the importance of evaluation in deploying LLM-based applications but does not provide specific examples or details related to what Vibe Testing is or its relevance to deployment. Therefore, it is considered less relevant to the given input.\"\n            }\n        ]\n    }\n]"}, "metric_configuration": {"threshold": 0.7, "evaluation_model": "Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "strict_mode": false, "include_reason": true}}, {"metric_data": {"name": "Faithfulness", "threshold": 0.7, "success": false, "score": 0.4, "reason": "The score is 0.40 because the actual output directly contradicts multiple claims made in the retrieval context regarding the importance and benefits of Vibe testing in AI development and validation processes.", "strictMode": false, "flaky": false, "evaluationModel": "Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "evaluationCost": 0, "verboseLogs": "Truths (limit=None):\n[\n    \"Deploying an LLM-based application without testing can lead to significant losses on the scale of a big company.\",\n    \"Vibe testing does not produce production-grade software in the industry.\",\n    \"Air Canada's chatbot incident highlighted the importance of deploying LLM-based applications through proper testing before release.\"\n] \n \nClaims:\n[\n    \"Vibe testing is a critical component of developing and validating artificial intelligence (LLM) models before deployment.\",\n    \"Vibe testing involves simulating user interactions with the model to ensure its performance, reliability, and correctness.\",\n    \"Vibe testing helps identify bugs, optimize parameters, and improve the overall quality of the model.\",\n    \"While vibe testing is essential for ensuring the robustness and accuracy of an LLM-based application, it alone is insufficient for deploying the model.\",\n    \"To fully validate an LLM app, additional steps such as thorough testing, rigorous validation processes, and continuous monitoring are required.\"\n] \n \nVerdicts:\n[\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": \"None\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"no\",\n        \"reason\": \"The retrieval context directly contradicts the first claim by stating that Vibe testing is a critical component of developing and validating AI models before deployment.\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"no\",\n        \"reason\": \"The retrieval context directly contradicts the second claim by stating that Vibe testing does not produce production-grade software in the industry.\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"no\",\n        \"reason\": \"The retrieval context directly contradicts the third claim by stating that Vibe testing helps identify bugs, optimize parameters, and improve the overall quality of the model.\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": \"None\"\n    }\n]"}, "metric_configuration": {"threshold": 0.7, "evaluation_model": "Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "strict_mode": false, "include_reason": true}}, {"metric_data": {"name": "Answer Relevancy", "threshold": 0.7, "success": false, "score": 0.6666666666666666, "reason": "The score is 0.67 because some irrelevant statements were present in the actual output, such as explaining why vibe testing alone is not sufficient for full deployment validation and reinforcing the importance of vibe testing without directly addressing what vibe testing is.", "strictMode": false, "flaky": false, "evaluationModel": "Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "evaluationCost": 0, "verboseLogs": "Statements:\n[\n    \"Vibe testing is a critical component of developing and validating artificial intelligence (LLM) models before deployment.\",\n    \"Vibe testing involves simulating user interactions with the model.\",\n    \"Vibe testing ensures the performance, reliability, and correctness of the model.\",\n    \"Vibe testing identifies bugs and optimizes parameters.\",\n    \"Vibe testing improves the overall quality of the model.\",\n    \"While vibe testing is essential for ensuring the robustness and accuracy of an LLM-based application, it alone is insufficient for deploying the model.\",\n    \"To fully validate an LLM app, additional steps such as thorough testing, rigorous validation processes, and continuous monitoring are required.\"\n] \n \nVerdicts:\n[\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": \"This statement addresses the importance of vibe testing in preparing an LLM app for deployment.\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"no\",\n        \"reason\": \"This statement explains why vibe testing alone is not sufficient for full deployment validation.\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": \"This statement elaborates on the need for additional steps beyond vibe testing.\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": \"This statement supports the idea that vibe testing is crucial but incomplete without other validations.\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"no\",\n        \"reason\": \"This statement reinforces the point that vibe testing is important but not enough for deployment.\"\n    }\n]"}, "metric_configuration": {"threshold": 0.7, "evaluation_model": "Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "strict_mode": false, "include_reason": true}}]}, "{\"actual_output\": \"The MMLU benchmark is a comprehensive evaluation framework designed to assess the capabilities of machine learning (ML) models. It consists of several components, including:\\n\\n1. **MMLU**: This is the original benchmark used since 2021. It includes 14,000 multiple-choice questions divided into 4 categories (MCQs). Each MCQ has 4 options, making it challenging for users to choose the correct answer quickly.\\n\\n2. **MMLU Pro**: This is a newer benchmark released in 2024. It offers a different approach to evaluating ML models compared to MMLU\", \"context\": null, \"expected_output\": null, \"hyperparameters\": null, \"input\": \"what is the mmlu benc