ls try to reach it this makes it clear that in this particular aspect in this particular problem benchmark models are reaching humans in MMLU Pro there was no such human baseline in the paper they did not give it, whereas in the original MMLU, people criticized that the benchmark you have designed why are you not carrying the core philosophy that's it, it is not a big point shall we move to the next ok the next benchmark is\", \"was done in the direction of depth of knowledge another direction was some more people thought that MMLU is a good benchmark even if it is saturated so let's do one thing so what they did was they made a new benchmark called MMLU Pro Pro is also from 2024 and what they did here they solved the problems of MMLU and made a new data set for example all the questions in MMLU 14000 questions were your MCQ and every MCQ had 4 options but in MMLU Pro every question had 10 options so here you have to find the right answer but in 10 given options so you can see that the difficulty level increased after this what they did is they reduced the number of subjects from 57 they came down if I remember correctly they came down to 12 subjects and in 12 subjects they got 12k questions so per subject 1000\", \"when you test two models then only you can say that scores are reliable this is a brief history of MMLU let me know if you are not able to understand if you want to read a detailed version of this then you can go to this website and read all this easily there is a lot of information here I have made an extract of this and pasted it here so to read everything you have to self study this website so you will have more knowledge so yeah let me know if you have any questions around this particular benchmark MMLU I will wait for one minute can you elaborate calibration point again you will understand in a while like we will do truthfulness discussion reliability discussion you will understand there now we will read a benchmark simple QA in simple QA we will di