ntext\": null, \"expected_output\": \"Custom model evals are evaluations you run on your own dataset to measure how well a model performs on your specific task, rather than on generic public benchmarks. You use them when standard benchmarks do not reflect your actual use case and you need to select the best model for your application. You build a dataset that represents your task and score candidate models on it to make the choice.\", \"hyperparameters\": null, \"input\": \"what are custom model evals and when would I use them instead of benchmarks?\", \"retrieval_context\": null}": {"cached_metrics_data": [{"metric_data": {"name": "Correctness [GEval]", "threshold": 0.7, "success": false, "score": 0.0, "reason": "The actual output does not address the question about when to use custom model evals instead of benchmarks.", "strictMode": false, "flaky": false, "evaluationModel": "Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "evaluationCost": 0, "verboseLogs": "Criteria:\nNone \n \nEvaluation Steps:\n[\n    \"Compare the actual answer with the expected answer.\",\n    \"Treat the expected answer as the reference answer.\",\n    \"Check whether the actual answer correctly addresses the question.\",\n    \"Do not require the wording to exactly match the expected answer.\",\n    \"Do not give credit for unsupported claims.\",\n    \"Judge factual correctness only.\"\n] \n \nRubric:\n0-4: The answer is substantially incorrect, contradicts the expected answer, or fails to answer the question.\n5-8: The answer is mostly correct but contains a minor error, omission, or imprecision.\n9-10: The answer is fully correct and directly addresses the question without substantive factual errors. \n \nScore: 0.0"}, "metric_configuration": {"threshold": 0.7, "evaluation_model": "Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "strict_mode": false, "include_reason": false, "evaluation_steps": ["Compare the actual answer with the expected answer.", "Treat the expected answer as the reference answer.", "Check whether the ac